# Let the desktop user switch the touchscreen's double tap to wake: the
# SM-X710's FTS1BA90A (samsung_fts1ba90a) and the SM-X910's Goodix GT6936
# (goodix-berlin-i2c, with this image's kernel patch).
#
# Both drivers create double_tap_to_wake root-only; the setting is off by
# default, as in the stock kernel, because armed it keeps the controller
# scanning in low-power mode while the screen is off and powered through
# system sleep.
# Only that attribute is opened up: power/wakeup (whether an armed gesture may
# also wake the system from sleep) stays with root.  The rule matches the
# drivers, so it does nothing on boards without these controllers, and the
# helper does nothing where the driver has no such attribute.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="i2c", DRIVER=="samsung_fts1ba90a|goodix-berlin-i2c", RUN+="/usr/libexec/ubuntu-gts9u-touch-permissions %p"
